==German==

===Etymology===
Backformation from the {{etym|nl|de}} plural {{term|Boeren|lang=nl}} from {{term|Boer|lang=nl}}. The word originally means “farmer” in Dutch but also in several German dialects, which is probably why the form ''Bur'' was avoided in German. (The word {{term|Bauer|lang=de}}, and even more ''Bur'' as a dialectal form, may have the pejorative implication of an illiterate person. Compare {{etym|en|-}} {{term|boor|lang=en}}.)

